%description:

RFC 9293 section 3.8.6.3, SHLD-18 -- a segment of 1 byte in an open window gets a delayed ACK.

The rule: "A TCP endpoint SHOULD implement a delayed ACK (SHLD-18)", with a delay of less than 0.5 s
(MUST-40). The receiver delays the ACK of a data segment that is neither out of order nor a full
segment, and sends it when the delay timer expires. Only a segment that is not acceptable gets an
ACK at once, such as a zero-window probe (section 3.10.7.4). The code treated each data segment of
1 byte as a possible persist probe and sent its ACK at once (BD-32 of the defect list).

Host B has delayed ACKs on, with the delay of 200 ms. Host A sends one byte into the open window of
host B at 0.2 s, and has nothing more to send. Host B sends nothing back.

Observation: host B sends no ACK of the byte for 0.19 s after the byte arrives, and sends it in the
next 0.05 s, when the delay timer has expired. An ACK at once is the fault.

Expected result: PASS.

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "PacketField.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

// At the TCP of a host a segment starts with its TCP header, so the data is what follows it.
static bool oneByteSegment(const MatchContext& context)
{
    const Packet *packet = context.event.packet;
    if (packet == nullptr)
        return false;
    return packet->getByteLength() - (long)evalPacketField(packet, "tcp.headerLength").doubleValueInUnit("B") == 1;
}

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("Rfc9293OneByteSegmentDelayedAck")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
                  .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
                  .describe("the SYN of host A")
                  .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
                  .filterEvent(oneByteSegment)
                  .first()
                  .describe("the segment of 1 byte arrives at host B, in an open window")
                  .within(1.0))
        .never(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                   .filterPacket("tcp.ackBit == true && tcp.synBit == false && tcp.ackNo == {isn} + 2")
                   .describe("the ACK of the byte before the delay timer of 200 ms expires")
                   .within(0.19))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.ackBit == true && tcp.synBit == false && tcp.ackNo == {isn} + 2")
                  .first()
                  .describe("the delayed ACK of the byte, when the timer has expired")
                  .within(0.05));
}

%activity:
EV << "Rfc9293OneByteSegmentDelayedAck compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.delayedAcksEnabled = true
*.host2.tcp.delayedAckTimeout = 200ms
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 1B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST Rfc9293OneByteSegmentDelayedAck: PASS
